MAME kiosk-no-ui, ported to mame0276 for the domainos station.

WHY A SEPARATE VARIANT. See mame-ctlsock-0276.patch's header — same story,
same station, same tag pin (docs/lab/DOMAINOS-WAVE.md "wall 1").

WHAT DIFFERS FROM mame-kiosk-no-ui.patch (0289)
  - src/emu/render.cpp: same MAME_NO_UI gate around the UI-container
    composition (`if (m_ui_container && !kh_no_ui)`), same
    `#include <cstdlib>` addition. Only the surrounding include block
    differs: 0.276's render.cpp includes "emu.h" then "render.h" directly
    with no intervening util/* headers, so the 0289 patch's first hunk (that
    inserts the include mid-way through a longer include block) does not
    match; the cstdlib include lands right after "emu.h" instead. The second
    hunk (the actual kh_no_ui logic, at "process UI elements if applicable")
    is otherwise identical — line numbers differ only because 0.276's file is
    shorter.

